[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Did You Want to Tell Me Something?]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:12.07]Why did the writer become very worried? | 为什么作者变得非常担忧？
[00:17.48]Dentists always ask questions when it is impossible for you to answer. | 牙科医生总是在你无法回答的时候向你提问。
[00:25.00]My dentist had just pulled out one of my teeth and had told me to rest for a while. | 我的牙科医生刚刚拔掉了我的一颗牙，让我休息一会儿。
[00:32.31]I tried to say something, | 我想说点什么，
[00:34.47]but my mouth was full of cotton wool. | 但我嘴里充满了药棉。
[00:38.40]He knew I collected match boxes and asked me whether my collection was growing. | 知道我收集火柴盒，他问我收藏是否在增加。
[00:44.89]He then asked me how my brother was and whether I liked my new job in London. | 接着他又问我的兄弟近况如何，问我是否喜欢在伦敦的新工作。
[00:52.98]In answer to these questions I either nodded or made strange noises. | 在回答这些问题时，我不是点头就是发出奇怪的声音。
[01:00.04]Meanwhile, my tongue was busy searching out the hole where the tooth had been. | 与此同时，我的舌头正忙着寻找刚拔掉的那颗牙的牙洞。
[01:06.94]I suddenly felt very worried, but could not say anything. | 我突然感到非常不安，但又什么也说不出来。
[01:13.52]When the dentist at last removed the cotton wool from my mouth, | 当那位牙医最后将药棉从我嘴中取出时，
[01:18.76]I was able to tell him that he had pulled out the wrong tooth. | 我总算能够告诉他，他拔错了牙。
